  <regions type="content">
    <region left="18" top="9" width="502" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">ASHRAE 2017 Moist Air Psychrometrics &amp; HVAC Engineering Calculations</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="45" width="91" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="false">2026-10-20</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="81" width="750" height="133" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">ASHRAE Handbook — Fundamentals (2017) Moist Air Psychrometrics Plugin for SMath Studio</p>
    <p bold="true">High-Precision Analytical &amp; Iterative Formulations for Building HVAC, Meteorology &amp; Process Design</p>
    <p bold="true">Native Assembly: PsychroLibWrapper.dll (Plugin GUID: 36a0265c-b529-4440-88e1-88f9226cee6a, v1.2.0.0)</p>
    <p bold="true">Strict SI Unit Guarantee: Pressure [Pa], Temperature [K], Enthalpy [J/kg] (m^2/s^2), Volume [m³/kg], Density [kg/m³]</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="225" width="748" height="412" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="false">The ASHRAE 2017 formulation represents the gold standard in building environmental engineering,</p>
    <p bold="false">meteorological science, and industrial drying/conditioning processes. It models moist air as an</p>
    <p bold="false">ideal mixture of dry air and water vapor, accurately accounting for the temperature dependence of</p>
    <p bold="false">saturation vapor pressure over liquid water (&gt; 0.01 °C) and ice (≤ 0.01 °C), barometric pressure</p>
    <p bold="false">variation with altitude, and non-linear enthalpy-humidity relations.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">Key Architectural Highlights of the PsychroLib SMath Plugin (v1.2.0.0 .NET 2.0 CLR):</p>
    <p bold="false">  1. 100% Pure Managed Execution: Zero external C runtimes or native wrappers; runs under Mono 6.14.1 on Linux.</p>
    <p bold="false">  2. Complete SI Standardization: All inputs/outputs strictly anchored to base SI units.</p>
    <p bold="false">  3. Bidirectional Temperature Transparency: Inputs accept Kelvin [K] or Celsius [°C] transparently;</p>
    <p bold="false">     outputs strictly return thermodynamic temperature in Kelvin [K].</p>
    <p bold="false">  4. Comprehensive 40-Function API: Clean Psy_&lt;Property&gt;_&lt;Inputs&gt; nomenclature covering dry air,</p>
    <p bold="false">     saturated air, moist air mixtures, altimetry, and backward inversions.</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="648" width="761" height="71" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">Section 1: Standard Atmosphere Altimetry &amp; Barometric Reductions</p>
    <p bold="true">Evaluation of ambient barometric pressure and temperature profiles from sea level to elevated sites (z = 1200 m).</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="729" width="122" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math decimalPlaces="4">
        <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
          <content>
        <p>HVAC project site elevation above mean sea level: 1200 m</p>
      </content>
        </description>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">z_site</e>
          <e type="operand">1200</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">m</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="792" width="412" height="25" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math decimalPlaces="4">
        <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
          <content>
        <p>Standard atmospheric pressure at 1200 m: 87715.52 Pa (0.877 bar)</p>
      </content>
        </description>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">p_atm_site</e>
          <e type="operand">z_site</e>
          <e type="function" args="1">Psy_AtmPressure</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">87715.5216</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">Pa</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
